<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sangkum Reastr Niyum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1955–1970</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sangkum Reastr Niyum, the People's Socialist Community, was the political movement founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> in 1955 after he abdicated the throne to enter politics. It won every seat in the National Assembly in the elections from 1955 to 1966 and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> under the banner of Buddhist socialism and neutrality in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>. It ended with Sihanouk's overthrow in 1970.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sangkum-reastr-niyum.jpg" alt="Sangkum Reastr Niyum" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_arms_of_Cambodia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
